{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic","id":1306534,"title":"The Supernal-Must-be-in-caste mechanic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-21T08:45:30-07:00","id":1306534,"title":"The Supernal-Must-be-in-caste mechanic","content":"To avoid derailing The aura thread more than it\u2019s already been derailed.<br /> <br /> So personally I don\u2019t see much value in limiting the supernal to the caste abilities? It basically massively reduces the scope of character concepts you can have at chargen, often with bizarre exclusions.<br /> <br /> You can\u2019t be a Twilight making an academic study of strategy with War.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Dawn caste admiral.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Zenith writing holy commandments into stone.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Dawn caste battle-sorcerer<br /> Burning Exorcism Technique is absolutely unavailable to a Zenith at chargen, as is any kind of high-essence medicine effect. Exorcism and healing the faithful isn\u2019t in theme for them?<br /> <br /> To be clear, I\u2019m not badmouthing the caste ability distribution. I think it works just fine. I just don\u2019t get why Supernal being limited to it is necessary or helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:02:51-07:00","id":1306538,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that it\u2019s partially game balance and partly to preserve some themes.<br /> <br /> Currently you can\u2019t be a Twilight with Survival Supernal, which is likely because being able to use all the familiar boosting charms on a Blood Ape or something would be hella broken right out of the gate.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, right now only Twilights can achieve the ultimate pinnacle of Craft right out of the gate, which cements their status as the preeminent craftspeople of the Exalted. You also have to be a Dawn if you want to do supernal violence to people, which reinforces their status as the preeminent combat specialists in Creation.<br /> <br /> Does this disable some starting options? Yes, but I think that it generally works well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:08:22-07:00","id":1306539,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on what you think those characters are doing with those abilities. You don't have to have Supernal in something to be good at it. I'll take just one example of this, your first one, but for most of them they basically fit into the same thing<br /> <br /> If the Twilight is making an academic study of War, do they need Supernal War? Why do they need access to charms past Essence 1 when at War 5 they're already one in tenthousands in terms of skill, and the addition of Solar Charms makes them better? If they're actually a general leading armies, they're a Dawn, if they're doing it for a scientific study basis, that reads more like someone who has general knowledge; why is Lore or Occult an unacceptable Supernal for them, with specialties in things like 'History of War' and 'Elemental Battle Tactics' plus War and some War charms? If the character is entirely focused on War and leading battles, they should probably be a Dawn. At Essence 1, any character who favors War can summon armies from nothing by bringing them to her call, she can train them to be immune to demoralization and ignore strategic maneuver penalties for being hungry, sick, or tired. The Solar can perfectly understand the terrain with a single glance, creating Strategic Maneuvers without knowing anything about their foe, double 9s to all command actions, and rally her forces with a single word. With just two of these effects and War 5, a Solar would already outclass almost any mortal general.<br /> <br /> I sort of agree with the Dawn thing and think it's silly that Sail is only Supernal for Eclipses, but that's really the only thing.<br /> <br /> In the same way as the first one, you don't need to have Linguistics Supernal to make a compelling message in a rock, especially when you have the ability to assign meaning to that message from your Presence and Performance, and you definitely don't need Craft Supernal to make a 10 Commandments style stone. With just a single charm purchase in Linguistics you have access to the decently powerful effect of doubling 9s with a 2 mote cost, to understand those speaking in tongues you don't understand for short bursts of time, and to communicate without speaking. In Craft you have exploding 10s, and a free Craft Excellency once per week. Major projects aren't that hard to complete, I would argue, and between those and, if you really want to go all out, Supreme Masterwork Focus' double 9s, you should be casually completing them. All at Essence 1.<br /> <br /> A Dawn can already start with Sorcery, Ghost-Eating Technique, and other powerful effects for exorcism which are available at Essence 1 without needing Occult Supernal.<br /> <br /> A Zenith at Essence 1 with Medicine Favored already has access to the ability to cleanse Plagues, even including the Great Contagion, with just a single charm and Attribute + Ability focus in that area.<br /> <br /> If you feel like one of these absolutely requires the Supernal addition of a different caste, the question is what makes them the caste that doesn't have it Supernal in the first place. If everyone could pick any Supernal, the Castes themselves would basically be meaningless, and people would just pick whatever has the best ability spread in Castes plus the best Caste Powers, rather then thinking of why their Exalt would be that caste.<br /> <br /> The current abilities already do a lot to offer this sort of 'cross-classing' by making very early charms incredibly powerful. To get caught up with 'yeah they're strong but I can't get (Insert Essence 5 Charm) so they aren't worth it' is missing the trees for the forest.<br /> <br /> It's also useful niche protection, because I remember late 2E where there was no reason for a Dawn to even show up because the Zenith could do all the things they did and didn't have to worry about 2-4 useless abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 04-21-2019, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:20:19-07:00","id":1306541,"title":"","content":"Zeniths aren\u2019t the only ones who can be priests of the Sun. They are simply the ones who are the Sun\u2019s priests automatically, even if they don\u2019t want to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:39:14-07:00","id":1306548,"title":"","content":"Yes, but exorcism seems like something a Zenith should be able to focus on as their main thing.<br /> <br /> I mean, I literally play a Zenith-caste exorcist monk. I have more Occult charms than anything else. But my Supernal ability is Integrity, because I'm a Zenith so I'm not allowed to have exorcism charms as Supernal (luckily, my Essence is 4, so it doesn't matter too much). I only actually have about 4 or 5 Integrity charms, whereas I have most of the Occult tree.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think sometimes Supernal being part of a particular Caste works well. It stops people from taking silly power-gamer combinations. You can't be a Twilight who's the greatest master of combat around, and you shouldn't be. Similarly, you can't be the greatest scholar around unless you're a Twilight.<br /> <br /> (And I think what inspired the Devs is the old Dawn problem; Dawns were not really that stand out in combat, so frequently if you wanted a character who was really good at combat, you wouldn't take a Dawn)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, while I don't really think a Twilight should be the greatest general around (what's wrong with a mental-primary, physical-tertiary Dawn?), sometimes stuff doesn't fit, no. A Zenith who is the most powerful exorcist around, a Dawn admiral, an Eclipse foot-courier*, these all seem like good concepts to me.<br /> <br /> *This is an example that came up in a game my friend's play. The ST decided to have a 2pt merit for people to take a non-Caste Supernal if appropriate, to have an Eclipse with Athletics-Supernal. But in fact... I don't think it worked very well from what I've heard, but from other reasons that lead into the whole issue of Castes and how restrictive they are because all concepts must fit into 5 archetypes. And to what extent restricting choices in order to inspire concepts and avoid broken bland messes, vs allowing choices to fit any concepts, is a good idea. Which maybe is a much bigger subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:40:51-07:00","id":1306550,"title":"","content":"I really don\u2019t think selecting a different Supernal is particularly breaking the game or undermining caste thematics. <br /> <br /> For one thing, the Familiar merit specifies that it refers to a beast of Creation, survival merits don\u2019t apply to demons.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit the twilight isn\u2019t the best example, but Sail being exclusive to Eclipses is plainly ridiculous, and absolutely undermines niches and thematics.<br /> <br /> Why? Because if a Dawn whose whole concept is their total domination of naval combat is attacked by an eclipse whose concept is the supremely efficient transportation of goods, they will go down like an absolute chump.<br /> You\u2019re right, if I wanted to make a Zenith around being supremely well written, I could just take the essence 1 charms and take, say, performance Supernal.<br /> <br /> My main two issues are that, again, while an eclipse\u2019s Linguistic mastery is perfectly in theme for them, They are also way better than my Zenith at the stuff that my Zenith Actually cares about.<br /> Also: I really don\u2019t want to take Supernal in an ability from which I don\u2019t particularly want high essence charms.<br /> <br /> Niche protection in terms of anima powers is debatable I guess, but I can say pretty definitively that Dawns no longer suffer from filling out every combat ability, and that their anima Power is far, far more suited to almost any combat build.<br /> Unless you specifically want to kill creatures of darkness, that sounds pretty Zenithy.<br /> <br /> Also just as a side note, Balance wise, a Supernal MA character has a stupendously expanded list of high essence charms to take. But that\u2019s only for Dawns.<br /> <br /> Which like, yeah. They\u2019re Dawns. Everyone here is Solars. balance is a weird proposition, but Supernal isn\u2019t going to combo with other caste abilities in any way that favored abilities wouldn\u2019t accomplish.<br /> <br /> The only real concern is Supernal comboing with Anima Powers. Which I guess they do a bit, but few things will be as useful as Melee comboing with a Decisve Reset Of 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-21-2019, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:47:28-07:00","id":1306553,"title":"","content":"An academic study of strategy would probably fall under Lore. Actually knowing about how to direct forces across battlefields and toward long-term objectives is somewhat different, not that it stopped Zhuge Liang and various other figures from having both ends covered to a great and profound degree in addition to their legendary inventing, statecraft, cooking, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:50:31-07:00","id":1306554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306550#post1306550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don\u2019t think selecting a different Supernal is particularly breaking the game or undermining caste thematics.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on if you're doing it because it fits your character or as a min-maxing power thing. Which... applies to a lot of stuff at character gen, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For one thing, the Familiar merit specifies that it refers to a beast of Creation, survival merits don\u2019t apply to demons. </div> </div> </div>Twilights can turn demons or elementals into Familiars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019ll admit the twilight isn\u2019t the best example, but Sail being exclusive to Eclipses is plainly ridiculous, and absolutely undermines niches and thematics.<br /> <br /> Why? Because if a Dawn whose whole concept is their total domination of naval combat is attacked by an eclipse whose concept is the supremely efficient transportation of goods, they will go down like an absolute chump. </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree with this. Though I'm not 100% sure the problem is that Dawns can't take Eclipse abilities as Supernal (I don't think it'd be appropriate for a Dawn to have Socialise Supernal or Linguistics Supernal). I wonder if actually the issue is that Sail should be a Dawn ability.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:58:30-07:00","id":1306555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306550#post1306550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don\u2019t think selecting a different Supernal is particularly breaking the game or undermining caste thematics.<br /> <br /> For one thing, the Familiar merit specifies that it refers to a beast of Creation, survival merits don\u2019t apply to demons.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit the twilight isn\u2019t the best example, but Sail being exclusive to Eclipses is plainly ridiculous, and absolutely undermines niches and thematics.<br /> <br /> Why? Because if a Dawn whose whole concept is their total domination of naval combat is attacked by an eclipse whose concept is the supremely efficient transportation of goods, they will go down like an absolute chump.<br /> You\u2019re right, if I wanted to make a Zenith around being supremely well written, I could just take the essence 1 charms and take, say, performance Supernal.<br /> <br /> My main two issues are that, again, while an eclipse\u2019s Linguistic mastery is perfectly in theme for them, They are also way better than my Zenith at the stuff that my Zenith Actually cares about.<br /> Also: I really don\u2019t want to take Supernal in an ability from which I don\u2019t particularly want high essence charms.<br /> <br /> Niche protection in terms of animal powers is debatable I guess, but I can say pretty definitively that Dawns no longer suffer from filling out every combat ability, and that their anima Power is far, far more suited to almost any combat build.<br /> Unless you specifically want to kill creatures of darkness, that sounds pretty Zenithy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't argue with Sail because I'm currently in a game where I want to have Sail Supernal for a Pirate King but am having issues fitting it into what I'm looking for otherwise. But I can discuss the other ones.<br /> <br /> Why is your Zenith a Zenith if they want to be distributing commands from on high through the diffusion of rules and laws rather then booming proclamations? those abilities fall into Socialize and can easily fit a Priest King Eclipse rather then a Zenith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306554#post1306554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely agree with this. Though I'm not 100% sure the problem is that Dawns can't take Eclipse abilities as Supernal (I don't think it'd be appropriate for a Dawn to have Socialise Supernal or Linguistics Supernal). I wonder if actually the issue is that Sail should be a Dawn ability.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more that only Eclipses can favor and thus Supernal Sail more then anything. If Either Dawns or Zeniths could, you'd have more flexibility in how you assign your caste. Especially since a lot of Sail is somewhere between War, Integrity, and Occult in how it functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:01:48-07:00","id":1306557,"title":"","content":"I can see why a Dawn's best ability would be Sail. But it doesn't really fit Zeniths to me.<br /> <br /> (I don't mean a Zenith can't be good at Sail. Just that I can't really see it as their most powerful ability.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:04:55-07:00","id":1306560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306557#post1306557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see why a Dawn's best ability would be Sail. But it doesn't really fit Zeniths to me.<br /> <br /> (I don't mean a Zenith can't be good at Sail. Just that I can't really see it as their most powerful ability.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see it either. I was thinking maybe something like Jason and his Argonauts as a support basis, where he's more bringing his friends along and providing moral support. Maybe Nights instead? To go with their other traveling abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:18:55-07:00","id":1306562,"title":"","content":"Just... as far as I can see this is a dual concern of avoiding game-breaking combos and and immersion-breaking concepts.<br /> <br /> The first one, I don\u2019t know. There\u2019s no combination of abilities with Supernal abilities that isn\u2019t accessible to anyone with access to that Supernal, so you\u2019re Just looking at Supernal/anima powers.<br /> <br /> If there\u2019s a combo in there that is truly, completely game-breaking I would I guess it\u2019s In Night caste. Once you get to essence 3 anyone can swallow their anima, but before that muting is handy. I don\u2019t think it substantially makes the game unfun broken though.<br /> <br /> As for the second...? Frankly, if I made a no moon lunar with a Lion spirit shape and by ST informed me that actually only Full Moons can have predator spirit shapes, that would be plain nonsense. My No Moon might be full strength DBT just Wrecking House, and nothing would prevent it from doing that completely and fully.<br /> <br /> And maybe if have a good reason to make that character No Moon or maybe I don\u2019t. That\u2019s resolvable in conversatiom about my character concept.<br /> There\u2019s a whole spread about how to make a Dawn, Zenith, Twilight, Night, or Eclipse. What they\u2019re about, how they do their thing. I\u2019m not going to Accidentally make a Supernal Sail Dawn into an Eclipse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-21-2019, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:33:41-07:00","id":1306566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306554#post1306554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twilghts can turn demons or elementals into Familiars.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok yeah I had not spotted that, and I\u2019ll admit that\u2019d combo well with high essence survival.<br /> I\u2019d say that just combining principle of motion with Essence Lending Method and its upgrade is a better use of that familiar but that is a combo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:39:17-07:00","id":1306569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306554#post1306554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely agree with this. Though I'm not 100% sure the problem is that Dawns can't take Eclipse abilities as Supernal (I don't think it'd be appropriate for a Dawn to have Socialise Supernal or Linguistics Supernal). I wonder if actually the issue is that Sail should be a Dawn ability.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There may exist a problem with Moray Darktide being a Dawn all the way since the Dawn book as an example of how to Dawn. It's not like Sail is super-defining of Eclipses, either; arguably, that would be Bureaucracy, which they nonetheless now share with Twilights (in addition to Linguistics), and Socialize, which is similarly on-dock for Nights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:51:26-07:00","id":1306573,"title":"","content":"(I\u2019m replying a Lot, sorry, just trying to get through responses, not trying to spam)<br /> <br /> As for a Linguistic Zenith, I mean, Perfect Recollection Discipline and Mind Scribing Method are both high essence linguistics charms that are also examples of miracles in several real-life holy texts. And I know Zeniths aren\u2019t Just priests that do priest things, but composing and memorising a a series of volumes on virtuous and proper living while wandering the desert or imprisoned for false heresy seems like an Extremely Zenith Thing to do?<br /> <br /> Like, I don\u2019t get that Shouting is a super Zenith thing to do to the exclusion of writing or engaging in rhetoric?<br /> It\u2019s not to say that eclipses shouldn\u2019t have linguistics or should have it less, Quite the opposite! Both approaches are solid, but only one is supported.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:05:32-07:00","id":1306576,"title":"","content":"Sail doesn't feel like a dawn ability to me.<br /> <br /> The thing is, dawns are largely in-your-face fighters. You can lead an army from the front, but you cant sail a ship whilst standing on the prow, punching other ships.<br /> <br /> And that's how a dawn pirate would work, in my eyes. Not the best sailor in the world. Just a passable one, who gets vaguely in range of enemy vessels, leaps on board and takes the crew out single handed.<br /> <br /> <i>Luffy</i> is a dawn. Luffy could not pilot his own ship for shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:08:28-07:00","id":1306577,"title":"","content":"Eye of the Unconquered Sun is a charm that reveals everyone and everything that is hiding or concealed in the Solar\u2019s vision, including disguises and disguising magic.<br /> <br /> How could that possibly serve Dawn thematics more than Twilight? In what way would a Supernal Awareness Twilight be thematically undercutting the Dawn or Night castes?<br /> <br /> And like, yeah. We can give Dawns Sail and Twilights Awareness and Zeniths Linguistics, and hopefully not mess up the balance of Caste abilities too much, Eclipses would be hard done by, but maybe they could get something else.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, we could leave caste abilities as they are and just remove a one sentence long rule, trusting that we\u2019ll be able to negotiate thematic characters without that limitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:15:51-07:00","id":1306578,"title":"","content":"I think there's a difference between changing a house rule at your table with an interaction with one player and character and a major rule being changed. If you're talking overall, then it'd be less weird and disruptive to overall change a few abilities around then to remove the Supernal rule, which I think adds a lot of flavor. I am just uncertain why you really require Supernal to be in certain abilities but not be in the Caste that requires them. If your Zenith is more focused on the writing portion of being imprisoned or wandering the desert to write a treaty, I simply have to ask again why they aren't an Eclipse, if so much of their concept focuses around their writings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:19:17-07:00","id":1306580,"title":"","content":"I <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306576#post1306576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, dawns are largely in-your-face fighters.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they\u2019re also the only caste that can be Supernal Archery.<br /> <br /> Heck, they can be Supernal Dodge if you want.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I don\u2019t think Dawns Do need sail. If I want a Sailin\u2019 Dawn, even a non-Supernal one, I can just take it as Favored.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think Zeniths need or should have Dodge as a Caste ability, but they\u2019re literally the only caste in which I can think of a concept for Supernal Dodge that I like. <br /> <br /> FWIW, a devotional ascetic who preserves the sanctity of their person by Never being touched. I think that\u2019s a solid way to fulfil the remit of Zeniths impressing and inspiring people into devotion to their virtue, and I don\u2019t think it\u2019s quite the same with performance Supernal and essence 1 dodge charms.<br /> <br /> Even if you don\u2019t think that\u2019s a particularly Zenith concept, is it less so than a Resistance Supernal Zenith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:24:19-07:00","id":1306582,"title":"","content":"Zenith who can't be touched feels more like something that would be done with a sort of pure aura, or that meditation charm (which is in caste)<br /> <br /> &quot;Zenith who matrix dodges any attempt to touch him&quot; just sounds ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:31:12-07:00","id":1306584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306578#post1306578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a difference between changing a house rule at your table with an interaction with one player and character and a major rule being changed. If you're talking overall, then it'd be less weird and disruptive to overall change a few abilities around then to remove the Supernal rule, which I think adds a lot of flavor. I am just uncertain why you really require Supernal to be in certain abilities but not be in the Caste that requires them. If your Zenith is more focused on the writing portion of being imprisoned or wandering the desert to write a treaty, I simply have to ask again why they aren't an Eclipse, if so much of their concept focuses around their writings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there\u2019s no possibility of Actually Changing the book. All of this discussion is only relevant to decisions between players and their ST. That\u2019s... if that wasn\u2019t clear: I don\u2019t actually want to book to be edited. I\u2019m just advocating for a change at the table that I use and I think is a good one. I wouldn\u2019t shift the caste distribution because I honestly don\u2019t think it needs to be moved. I don\u2019t think Dawns should have Sail as a caste ability.<br /> <br /> To the second point, castes aren\u2019t their abilities. Eclipses are described as Diplomats, Explorers, Merchants, and Organisers. Zeniths are described as Firebrands, Orators, Rebels, Priests, and Moral Constants.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s pretty plain that the character described isn\u2019t diplomatic, mercantile, or exploratory. So why would I place them in a caste that is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:34:33-07:00","id":1306586,"title":"","content":"The guy you described as wandering the desert to compose his treatise on proper living isn't exploratory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:39:03-07:00","id":1306589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306582#post1306582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zenith who can't be touched feels more like something that would be done with a sort of pure aura, or that meditation charm (which is in caste)<br /> <br /> &quot;Zenith who matrix dodges any attempt to touch him&quot; just sounds ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. I thought it was cool but honestly I was just trying to think of any kind of Supernal Dodge character and Zenith was the best I could come up with. Can you honestly describe a more apt Night caste with Supernal Dodge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-21-2019, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:41:32-07:00","id":1306590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306586#post1306586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guy you described as wandering the desert to compose his treatise on proper living isn't exploratory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the intention was that he wasn\u2019t there on purpose, I did also give being imprisoned as an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:42:28-07:00","id":1306591,"title":"","content":"The gentleman thief who can dodge between raindrops, who refuses to raise a hand to his defense but will humiliate those attacking him with his graceful movements and taunting words?<br /> <br /> It could be any number of Night abilities but Dodge is one of them.<br /> <br /> Edit; and the person imprisoned by being forced to wander the desert is in a great place to be assaulted by raiding Fae only to fall under the auspicious protection of the Sun, able to avoid their tempting words and them unable to strike her as she wanders","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 04-21-2019, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:44:05-07:00","id":1306592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306538#post1306538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that it\u2019s partially game balance and partly to preserve some themes.<br /> <br /> Currently you can\u2019t be a Twilight with Survival Supernal, which is likely because being able to use all the familiar boosting charms on a Blood Ape or something would be hella broken right out of the gate.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, right now only Twilights can achieve the ultimate pinnacle of Craft right out of the gate, which cements their status as the preeminent craftspeople of the Exalted. You also have to be a Dawn if you want to do supernal violence to people, which reinforces their status as the preeminent combat specialists in Creation.<br /> <br /> Does this disable some starting options? Yes, but I think that it generally works well.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? I personally hate supernal as a mechanic but how is that different from a zenith who wants to do that? Nothing actually stops him from doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:49:34-07:00","id":1306595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306592#post1306592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How? I personally hate supernal as a mechanic but how is that different from a zenith who wants to do that? Nothing actually stops him from doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it means you can't pick up the big Essence 3-5 charms that make the creature immune to being crashed and stuff until you actually get to that Essence ele","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:50:10-07:00","id":1306596,"title":"","content":"Moray Darktide always seemed odd to me that he's brought up. Since while, yes he's a sailor and pirate, that he's Exatled as a Dawn to me should indicate what his definings trenghts are. He can still favor Sail and be a badass. But the Sun didn't Choose him to be the ultimate Sailor, he Chose him to be the ultimate <i>Warrior</i>. And so as noted upthread a bit, he's probably Supernaling Melee (he does have a badass katana there) or something. Because he was Chosen as a fighter or commander first, not Sailor.<br /> <br /> I guess to me that's the big where it is a bit on setting-immersion. I actually just don't see Sail as a very Dawn Ability as it's about commanding a machine, maneuveirng and all that. Actually fighting, firing weapons, commanding troops, all that are the Dawn things, and you can do those <i>and</i> be a good sailor. It's just that he aspects of your legend are defined with piloting a boat. Which well, I don't see that as very Dawn. The swashbuckling badass fighting on teh decks and leading the baording party is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:58:40-07:00","id":1306601,"title":"","content":"The thing is that Sail does also include warlike stuff. It includes charms to modify and boost the strategic maneuver actions on Sail, to make your crew into swashbuckling soldiers, and doesn't your Sail score limit your War for the purposes of strategic maneuvers while you're on a boat?<br /> <br /> Sail isn't just about piloting, it has charms for being a fearless swashbuckler and being a captain leading a crew of raiders from the front and being great at forcing your boat opponents into traps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T12:04:35-07:00","id":1306602,"title":"","content":"Ok, I think I see the disconnect here.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m coming at Castes from a point of view of Motivation and Purpose. That was honestly my main read on them. So if I see a way for a non-caste ability to express that purpose in an interesting manner, I\u2019d rather have access to it. And that\u2019s how I\u2019m going to play.<br /> <br /> And I guess the other point of view is that casts are defined by the abilities, that regardless of what you\u2019re doing or why, the actual medium by which you accomplish it is the definitional nature of your caste. Regardless of whether you pirate or trade or make war or seek out oceanic secrets, you\u2019re an Eclipse because you sail.<br /> Honestly that doesn\u2019t appeal to me so I probably haven\u2019t expressed it with a lot of poetry, but I can respect it. Fair enough,<br /> <br /> Oh and I do like the gentleman thief concept. Sorry you don\u2019t like the dodge-Zenith, I was thinking a sort of Pai-Mei with more spirituality and less being a dickhead type of thing,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T12:17:10-07:00","id":1306604,"title":"","content":"Agree it is constraining to some degree. It seems like if you want to be a crafter of swords as your highest, distinctive character peak, but generally a warrior, or the greatest tactician as your defining peak, but otherwise generally a smart guy who is good at smart guy type stuff (and not a warrior), this isn't really so much a Solar space (at least at chargen), as in previous editions?<br /> <br /> Not to dislike the concept of the Supernal Ability, as pretty cool as a distinctive way to pace the Solar curve - it fulfills the promise that they are &quot;The Best&quot; (tm) at some ability from chargen and paces their growth more around filling out as they get more Essence (which is a distinct curve from just getting better proportionately in everything). But yeah, the 3e characters that chargen pushes your towards seem different than previous editions without further distinction between Caste / Favored. Feature or bug is to taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T12:59:38-07:00","id":1306610,"title":"","content":"I'm broadly in favour of Caste Supernal. Its helped me realise some baggage and unspoken assuptions that myself and others have towards the Solar Castes.<br /> For example, there's this deeply rooted notion of the Dawn Caste as dumb muscle that I still occasionally see signs of when Martial Arts comes up due to a combination of its in-setting connection to enlightenment and RL notions of the scrawny kid learning martial arts to fight back against people who are bigger and hit harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T13:43:27-07:00","id":1306627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306595#post1306595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it means you can't pick up the big Essence 3-5 charms that make the creature immune to being crashed and stuff until you actually get to that Essence ele</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's okay for a zenith to do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T13:56:52-07:00","id":1306633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306627#post1306627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it's okay for a zenith to do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Zenith can't do it to a Blood Ape or other powerful Demon slash Spirit. At least not right away","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T14:56:41-07:00","id":1306649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306601#post1306601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that Sail does also include warlike stuff. It includes charms to modify and boost the strategic maneuver actions on Sail, to make your crew into swashbuckling soldiers, and doesn't your Sail score limit your War for the purposes of strategic maneuvers while you're on a boat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sail has no effect on your ablity to do strategic manuevering as I can read on the rules. In fact, once you board a ship and are actually fighting, the rules say to just use normal combat, and that's about it. This seems to tie in with how I think on things a bit. The game rules as they are separate being a good navigator/pilot of a ship from being a good strategist in actual fights. The mechanics as they are separate what it takes to be a good tactical sailor from a good tactician.<br /> <br /> That there is combat applicaiton of Sail and Dawns don't get it is a matter of a few things to me. 1) They wanted eight Abilites for each Caste, Dawns got their original five and the three they got as well are things that are pretty good associations with them and say something of the kind of characters that fit it. And 2) Reality and ficiton don't 1:1 cut along game mechanic joints, and so while there are some things in Sail that have a Dawn-like look, they don't justify giving Dawns the entire Sail Ability carte blanche if there is also a want to make sure a Castes overarching themes fit best besides specifics of mechanical overlap. A bit to me is what the Sail rules to me read as in 3e, where they are about your competence of actually commanding the ship. Being a good tactician tells you you should baord a ship. Being a good navigator/pilot lets you do that. Those are represented separately in the system. Just liike knowing when to hide is good tactics, but the Children of the Dawn are not the sorts who are known to be pinnacle of hiding amongst the Chosen. And the system somewhat shows this a bit. Dawns don't normally Supernal Sail because the mechancis themselves are not really as much about knowing what to do, but you doing them.<br /> <br /> (I'd argue that this is probably actually a flaw somewhat of the Sail mechanics amongst other things they have for being underdeveloped, mathed badly, and having too many Charms that mess wiht that math that break it further but that's another argument).<br /> <br /> To me, Moray as an admiral is the kind of guy who knows when to strike, who picks his battles, and is probably still good enough with the most powerful dice trick Solars have (their Excellency) to get most things done to get to his personal strengths of fights on actual ships and looting. Or, he's good enough that he's able to get navigators and helmsmen that are able to compliment his strenghts as a tactician.<br /> <br /> Sail isn't just about piloting, it has charms for being a fearless swashbuckler and being a captain leading a crew of raiders from the front and being great at forcing your boat opponents into traps. This is a bit why I generally find it kind of a weak arguemnt for the non-Caste Supernal stuff. Moray was likely Exalted because well, he was a good general or warrior, not because he was good helmsman. The system reflects that and I think that there's a conflation of the helmsman with the swashbuckler I'm not sure is warranted here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306601#post1306601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sail isn't just about piloting, it has charms for being a fearless swashbuckler and being a captain leading a crew of raiders from the front and being great at forcing your boat opponents into traps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting up those traps, and such on the long term are the domain of Strategic Warfare. Once teh ships are like, there and trying to maneuver, that's the Sail Maneuvering system. That's the domain fo helmsmen, not tacticians, although a good tactician might know the best course of action, again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T14:58:34-07:00","id":1306651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306604#post1306604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree it is constraining to some degree. It seems like if you want to be a crafter of swords as your highest, distinctive character peak, but generally a warrior, or the greatest tactician as your defining peak, but otherwise generally a smart guy who is good at smart guy type stuff (and not a warrior), this isn't really so much a Solar space (at least at chargen), as in previous editions?<br /> <br /> Not to dislike the concept of the Supernal Ability, as pretty cool as a distinctive way to pace the Solar curve - it fulfills the promise that they are &quot;The Best&quot; (tm) at some ability from chargen and paces their growth more around filling out as they get more Essence (which is a distinct curve from just getting better proportionately in everything). But yeah, the 3e characters that chargen pushes your towards seem different than previous editions without further distinction between Caste / Favored. Feature or bug is to taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, nothing stops a Twlight from being a warrior. You get five Supernals. Unless you mean as generally as a Dawn, probably not. But than again, if you were going to be running around wanting three forms of killing folks as Abiliites, were you actually that interested in having Craft do a lot or are you just spreading yourself thin hypothetically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T15:12:30-07:00","id":1306657,"title":"","content":"Supernal limits are removed with the greatest of ease.<br /> <br /> There was an idea behind limiting them by Caste. It's not going to be to everybody's taste, and it's not a travesty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306569#post1306569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There may exist a problem with Moray Darktide being a Dawn all the way since the Dawn book as an example of how to Dawn. It's not like Sail is super-defining of Eclipses, either; arguably, that would be Bureaucracy, which they nonetheless now share with Twilights (in addition to Linguistics), and Socialize, which is similarly on-dock for Nights.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The signature Eclipse is a far-riding Delzhan.<br /> <br /> They're world-walkers in addition to socialites.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T15:30:49-07:00","id":1306662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306651#post1306651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, nothing stops a Twlight from being a warrior. You get five Supernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I suppose there is the workaround, say, (to go with my other example) you wanted to play the extremely smart Supernal tactician with no other major martial prowess, of playing a Dawn that buys War, spends nothing on any of his chosen Dawn Abilities, and then spends everything on his Favored Abilities, which are Twilight Abilities. It's something that the system is nudging against though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T15:38:12-07:00","id":1306663,"title":"","content":"I definitely think that the &quot;Sail&quot; problem is the naval mechanics more than Solar admirals not being able to take Sail Supernal.<br /> <br /> Why don't people bring up Solar not having Ride as a Supernal option? Mastering fighting while mounted sounds like a Dawn thing, and there are certainly great warriors for inspiration for a Dawn that focuses on Ride.<br /> <br /> The reason is simple. A Supernal Melee/Ride Favored Dawn, and a Supernal Ride/Melee Favored Eclipse perform differently at start, but because of the combat system, you don't feel left out going with whichever suits your concept better. If you want to play a mounted spear user, you're going to have high Melee and high Ride, and want lots of Charms from both... your Supernal is just which you start higher up on (and it would be even if it wasn't Caste linked).<br /> <br /> If War had more impact on the naval mechanics, then the Dawn admiral concept would be War Supernal and Sail Favored, and it wouldn't feel weird at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T16:21:44-07:00","id":1306672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306662#post1306662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, I suppose there is the workaround, say, (to go with my other example) you wanted to play the extremely smart Supernal tactician with no other major martial prowess, of playing a Dawn that buys War, spends nothing on any of his chosen Dawn Abilities, and then spends everything on his Favored Abilities, which are Twilight Abilities. It's something that the system is nudging against though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, in 3e, if you want to be the brainy tactician who doesn't htemself fight...you do that as a Zenith. They can favor Lore and War just fine, and also are good at getting folks to follow them and keeping cool when shit goes awry. Which I think is something to consider a bit too. Castes have quite a lot of gorund they can cover now, including with how soem Abilities that were &quot;Twligiht&quot; or whatever, arne't exclusivley so anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T17:33:28-07:00","id":1306688,"title":"","content":"I realize I'm a latecomer to the thread (that's what I get for passing out), but being super-invested in an Ability <i>hardly</i> necessitates getting higher than Essence 1 Charms for it; my Eclipse is Socialize Supernal, but his Investigation dots are equally beefy, and he's done about as much with both. I don't think I've even used all my Socialize Charms yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-21-2019, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T18:46:44-07:00","id":1306707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306577#post1306577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eye of the Unconquered Sun is a charm that reveals everyone and everything that is hiding or concealed in the Solar\u2019s vision, including disguises and disguising magic.<br /> <br /> How could that possibly serve Dawn thematics more than Twilight? In what way would a Supernal Awareness Twilight be thematically undercutting the Dawn or Night castes?<br /> <br /> And like, yeah. We can give Dawns Sail and Twilights Awareness and Zeniths Linguistics, and hopefully not mess up the balance of Caste abilities too much, Eclipses would be hard done by, but maybe they could get something else.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, we could leave caste abilities as they are and just remove a one sentence long rule, trusting that we\u2019ll be able to negotiate thematic characters without that limitation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think Dawns have Awareness because of its synergy with Archery, which is also their thing. They are Masters of not only close combat but also range with Thrown and Archery. While the Eye isn't really necessary for that sort of thing that Solars would need it, as so far the other charms in awareness. In allowing your sense to extremely expand and allowing you to see through any ambush. That I think fits Dawn. <br /> <br /> The thing of what I think Supernal is that I like it, I see it fits what it needs to do and its fitting. Now I also understand that it does limit from some other thematic stuff but from the way I see it just allowing it to apply to any ability isn't the way to go about it. Really the way I would do it is just expand the list. Their are 25 abilities and each Caste gets 8, if that is limiting your concept then move it to 10 for example, give everyone 2 more favored abilities. For me, I see Thrown as being very fitting for night, with all its sneakyness in the charms, but I also see that there is few else I see Nights really missing. I don't want to lose the focus that Supernal brings to the themes of the Caste and as people noted out you really don't need that much investment in other abilities to do cool stuff, thats how I would go about it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T18:53:45-07:00","id":1306710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306657#post1306657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal limits are removed with the greatest of ease.<br /> <br /> There was an idea behind limiting them by Caste. It's not going to be to everybody's taste, and it's not a travesty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I mean maybe I\u2019m getting a bit heated about character concepts I find cool, but I\u2019m not trying to tear down Eclipses that can fight things in boats or Dawns that are extremely perceptive.<br /> <br /> I guess I just can\u2019t see that the intentions behind limited Supernal selection are borne out by the caste distribution and the rest of the book.<br /> <br /> Protecting thematic caste abilities: There\u2019s nothing more Night Caste than muting your anima, and yet a Supernal Larceny Eclipse is fully capable of muting peripherals used in any larceny action at least twice per scene. For free, at that.<br /> <br /> Preserving game balance: look this is difficult, I could argue that a Demon familiar is better served by occult charms than Survival, particularly in terms of Materialising. But balance is kind of weird to address when Dawns are and should be the Best Combatant Caste.<br /> <br /> Like, a materialised Erymanthus with Survival empowerment is formidable. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s quite as dangerous as a Supernal archer with range and a vantage point. Add athletics which is also In caste and the Dawn charm resets and it\u2019s not even a question.<br /> <br /> That said, if you find it does achieve this goals, absolutely go for it. I literally cannot stop you and wouldn\u2019t if I could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T19:02:17-07:00","id":1306714,"title":"","content":"Athletics isn't a Dawn Caste Ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T19:31:48-07:00","id":1306718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306710#post1306710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Protecting thematic caste abilities: There\u2019s nothing more Night Caste than muting your anima, and yet a Supernal Larceny Eclipse is fully capable of muting peripherals used in any larceny action at least twice per scene. For free, at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't see it as making the Castes feel intrinsically different from one another so much as making the Castes feel more like themselves.<br /> <br /> Take the Dawn Caste. There are arguably Abilities that might make sense for them as further Caste Abilities, and some might feel that some of those are more fitting than some of the expansions that they were actually given. For the former, I'd say that when the Castes are given only eight, something ends up on the cutting room floor. For the latter, well, not everybody is going to have the same ideas (and maybe there was an intention to not have some Abilities show up too little or too often); I'd say they're easy enough to shift around.<br /> <br /> But I'd also say that there are Abilities that are fairly far afield from the Dawn Caste, excepting very narrow applications, and letting them be Supernal in place of something for combat would be off. At the same time, Favoured Abilities are something that has value in being a mode for development and characterisation stretching way from Caste.<br /> <br /> Not everybody has much regard for Caste, but between deeper Anima powers and the significance given to it for experience points, I'd say that it's something this Edition is giving a prominence to. So it's the apparent basis for giving Solars a means of expanding vertically early on. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T19:35:23-07:00","id":1306719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic#post1306534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To avoid derailing The aura thread more than it\u2019s already been derailed.<br /> <br /> So personally I don\u2019t see much value in limiting the supernal to the caste abilities? It basically massively reduces the scope of character concepts you can have at chargen, often with bizarre exclusions.<br /> <br /> You can\u2019t be a Twilight making an academic study of strategy with War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, because that's what Dawns do. This particular complaint makes little sense unless you just assume Dawns are nothing but idiot meatheads that bash things till they die. There is literally nothing preventing you from having an intelligent academically-focused Dawn with Supernal War .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T19:53:03-07:00","id":1306725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic#post1306534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can\u2019t be a Twilight making an academic study of strategy with War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously this isn't true. You're still very able to Favor War and put dots in it and buy <i>seven</i> War Charms right off the bat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic#post1306534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can\u2019t be a Dawn caste admiral.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are <i>twelve</i> Essence 1 Sail Charms. There's no Charm prerequisite for being an admiral.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic#post1306534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can\u2019t be a Zenith writing holy commandments into stone.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Ten</i> Essence 1 Linguistics Charms. Also all it takes to know how to write is Linguistics 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic#post1306534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can\u2019t be a Dawn caste battle-sorcerer</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only is every Terrestrial Circle spell available at Essence 1, having Occult Supernal doesn't even get you any more access to sorcery than Joe Non-Supernal Occult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic#post1306534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Burning Exorcism Technique is absolutely unavailable to a Zenith at chargen, as is any kind of high-essence medicine effect. Exorcism and healing the faithful isn\u2019t in theme for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Zenith anima power lets them force a spirit to materialize. Moreover, even if they didn't have that, Phantom-Seizing Strike and Ghost-Eating Technique are all still Essence 1, as well as the option to pick up the exorcism thaumaturgy ritual, considering you get the thaumaturgy merit for free when you take Terrestrial Circle Sorcery.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, <b>you can cure a person of the Great Contagion with only Essence 1 Solar Charms.</b> I can't stress that enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-21-2019, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T20:12:52-07:00","id":1306728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306657#post1306657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal limits are removed with the greatest of ease.<br /> <br /> There was an idea behind limiting them by Caste. It's not going to be to everybody's taste, and it's not a travesty.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The signature Eclipse is a far-riding Delzhan.<br /> <br /> They're world-walkers in addition to socialites.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>And Nights can have Ride in-caste. That the other travel Ability didn't get to anyone else seems more like Blaque's mention of priorities in Ability distribution than to actual signature traits of the Caste, especially since that selfsame signature Eclipse doesn't seem to have or care about Sail, but there has been an emphasis on Eclipses being behind the scenes operators since the inception of the game.<br /> <br /> (Also, Abyssals and Infernals are apparently going to get different expanded options for the equivalent Solar Castes; Dusks getting Ride was one example.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T20:12:52-07:00","id":1306729,"title":"","content":"Double post, ignore. Could have sworn that I only pressed send once...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T20:39:10-07:00","id":1306735,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to treat the rule as a guideline - basically players can always take a Caste Ability as Supernal, but they can request to take another one if it really fits their concept and just need to justify it to me first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T22:15:18-07:00","id":1306757,"title":"","content":"Hey all, I think I went a bit far in defence of this notion, so I just want to apologise if I was dismissive or narrow minded in responding. Certainly the double posting was a bit much.<br /> <br /> I do think that an out of caste Supernal is perfectly acceptable in negotiation with your ST, but I also see where y\u2019all are coming from, and I\u2019m not meaning to knock it.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t argue the point anymore, because I\u2019m getting worked up over it when there\u2019s really no need to.<br /> <br /> Your examples there are solid, Countalucard, and I would say that if your concept fits with a Supernal that Is available to you, absolutely that should be your first choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T22:27:04-07:00","id":1306759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306757#post1306757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your examples there are solid, Countalucard, and I would say that if your concept fits with a Supernal that Is available to you, absolutely that should be your first choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were <i>your</i> examples. They were in the first post in the thread and everything - all I did was show how you don't need a non-Caste Ability to be Supernal for you to still be largely defined by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T22:36:38-07:00","id":1306760,"title":"","content":"What I got out of this discussion is that Sail probably should be a Dawn Caste ability because it does apply to combat on the high seas as much as war applies to leading armies, and Dawns got dodge and Resistance because they are common combat abilities and not because they are thematically appropriate. I'd probably swap Resistance for Sail on the Dawn caste list, as there aren't really any non-combat related uses for dodge, if I felt that it mattered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T22:51:01-07:00","id":1306764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306759#post1306759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were <i>your</i> examples. They were in the first post in the thread and everything - all I did was show how you don't need a non-Caste Ability to be Supernal for you to still be largely defined by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I... I was agreeing with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T02:45:18-07:00","id":1306785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306719#post1306719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yes, because that's what Dawns do. This particular complaint makes little sense unless you just assume Dawns are nothing but idiot meatheads that bash things till they die. There is literally nothing preventing you from having an intelligent academically-focused Dawn with Supernal War .</div> </div> </div> </div>This has come up a couple of times on this thread, so I want to reinforce what Frostav has says.<br /> <br /> Full Moons are the physical attribute caste. While its technically possible to make a Full Moon who's physical tertiary, it's a bit awkward.<br /> <br /> Dawns are not, that just tends to be common.<br /> A brilliant strategist who directs his armies from the back, out-reading and out-maneouvering his enemies, is a Dawn, not a Twilight. (At least, if that's his main focus.)<br /> <br /> Similarly, a Twilight could be burly and physical. Perhaps they're an amazing smith, the best in the land, with huge muscles but little book-learning. Supernal Craft, favour Athletics and Melee.<br /> <br /> It's actually No Moons who are the Intelligence-favouring Caste, after all, not Twilights. Hey, when I played a Twilight, I don't think he was even mental primary.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What I got out of this discussion is that Sail probably should be a Dawn Caste ability because it does apply to combat on the high seas as much as war applies to leading armies, and Dawns got dodge and Resistance because they are common combat abilities and not because they are thematically appropriate. I'd probably swap Resistance for Sail on the Dawn caste list,</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... I think Resistance fits. We have a Resistance-Supernal Dawn in his huge heavy armour, it makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> I actually would take out Awareness. But tbh, I think it's a hard one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as there aren't really any non-combat related uses for dodge, if I felt that it mattered. </div> </div> </div> Avoiding traps? I can't think of anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">having Occult Supernal doesn't even get you any more access to sorcery than Joe Non-Supernal Occult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, people always forget Occult is not really about sorcery, it's about spirits and exorcism.<br /> <br /> Still, Alucard, while I see your point about being able to take a bunch of Essence 1 charms anyway, and it is a good point... if your point is &quot;it doesn't matter that you can't take Supernal&quot; then what's even the point of Supernal at all?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T03:07:52-07:00","id":1306787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306662#post1306662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, I suppose there is the workaround, say, (to go with my other example) you wanted to play the extremely smart Supernal tactician with no other major martial prowess, of playing a Dawn that buys War, spends nothing on any of his chosen Dawn Abilities, and then spends everything on his Favored Abilities, which are Twilight Abilities. It's something that the system is nudging against though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do more with the ability spread if you move away from the traditional Dawn Caste ones Awareness, Resistance and Dodge all have things to offer that could be in service to this concept.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T05:06:30-07:00","id":1306801,"title":"","content":"Yeah, true, there are quite a few things that you can do to shape the chosen Caste Ability spread around the character as well. I suppose some of this is that it feels odd to me to be choosing the key strength you're interested in as a player, and then pick the caste dependent on that, and then try and shape general ability profile, and the Caste specific narrative (mainly around past lives) in line with that constraint. Rather than just picking your Caste somewhat independently of that concern (as in previous editions, where you did choose for a Solar PC to have a key strength at all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T06:46:11-07:00","id":1306830,"title":"","content":"I think possibly the issue is that the devs felt that the key strength of a character and the genre-narrative of that caste would always go together, so picking them would seamlessly match.<br /> And often, especially with common concepts, it does. Dawn swordsman, Eclipse courtier, Night thief, Twilight scholar, etc.<br /> <br /> But no character gen system is perfect, and sometimes they don't connect together. And then you get the situation where some players choose their caste based on the supernal, not the narrative, which gets a bit odd.<br /> The same thing happens with Role bonuses though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T07:09:26-07:00","id":1306838,"title":"","content":"I think there are always interesting concepts cut short by character creation being limited, but I also think those limitations can force you to look at a character in a new light and even come at concepts from different angles.<br /> <br /> For instance, one character archetype I've wanted to play for awhile is a Swordsmansmith, who masters their craft of sword making by using the swords they make, then refining them over and over. Obviously such a character could be either a Dawn with Melee or a Twilight with Craft. And I think because there's a limit on Supernals, that concept could be viewed entirely differently based on which caste you pick and which Supernal you take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T07:31:05-07:00","id":1306846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306728#post1306728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Nights can have Ride in-caste. That the other travel Ability didn't get to anyone else seems more like Blaque's mention of priorities in Ability distribution than to actual signature traits of the Caste, especially since that selfsame signature Eclipse doesn't seem to have or care about Sail, but there has been an emphasis on Eclipses being behind the scenes operators since the inception of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swan came from the West, didn't he?<br /> <br /> He seems to me to have been more of a world-walker than he was a behind-the-scenes operator.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T09:31:22-07:00","id":1306864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306785#post1306785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... I think Resistance fits. We have a Resistance-Supernal Dawn in his huge heavy armour, it makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> I actually would take out Awareness. But tbh, I think it's a hard one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest awareness is such a poor fit that I forgot Dawn's get it, so I picked dropping resistance over dodge. Awareness is definitely the one to drop. It's kinda weird to have it classes a combat ability because that just so happens to be mechanically where Join Battle suits. Its definitely not an iconic awareness thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T09:34:39-07:00","id":1306865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic#post1306534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To avoid derailing The aura thread more than it\u2019s already been derailed.<br /> <br /> So personally I don\u2019t see much value in limiting the supernal to the caste abilities? It basically massively reduces the scope of character concepts you can have at chargen, often with bizarre exclusions.<br /> <br /> You can\u2019t be a Twilight making an academic study of strategy with War.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Dawn caste admiral.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Zenith writing holy commandments into stone.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Dawn caste battle-sorcerer<br /> Burning Exorcism Technique is absolutely unavailable to a Zenith at chargen, as is any kind of high-essence medicine effect. Exorcism and healing the faithful isn\u2019t in theme for them?<br /> <br /> To be clear, I\u2019m not badmouthing the caste ability distribution. I think it works just fine. I just don\u2019t get why Supernal being limited to it is necessary or helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this can be solved easily by applying the Golden Rule, pg 182 of Ex3 core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don\u2019t like one of these rules,<br /> change it. If a rule is getting in the way of having fun,<br /> throw it out. If you have an idea that would work better<br /> for your group than one of the rules here, go with that.<br /> Nobody knows better than you what you\u2019ll find fun. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T09:41:08-07:00","id":1306867,"title":"","content":"I mean, that's always the case. The thread is really whether it's good for the game to change. Of course, at your table you can change anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:21:57-07:00","id":1306914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306785#post1306785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, Alucard, while I see your point about being able to take a bunch of Essence 1 charms anyway, and it is a good point... if your point is &quot;it doesn't matter that you can't take Supernal&quot; then what's even the point of Supernal at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point is more, &quot;Supernal doesn't matter as much as people are making it out to.&quot; Supernal matters because it lets you gain access to higher level Charms early, and that's a significant impact on play. It's just something that isn't essential, and something that matters less and less as time goes on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:16:45-07:00","id":1306935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306865#post1306865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this can be solved easily by applying the Golden Rule, pg 182 of Ex3 core.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Rule zero isn't exactly useful for discussion in a public forum. The rules form the common basis by which all discussions take place. Even in private use the golden rule can serve as an obstacle to bringing in new people to game as they understand the game in terms of the published rules. Really, I consider all 3 for those rules to be absolutely terrible, so I avoid them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T14:42:49-07:00","id":1306985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306865#post1306865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this can be solved easily by applying the Golden Rule, pg 182 of Ex3 core.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah but of course XD<br /> I think there\u2019s a lot of \u201cwhy would you ever\u201d/\u201cwhy would you ever not\u201d, and obviously that\u2019s going to come down to your taste and your table.<br /> I know that some people (myself included) start most solar concepts by thinking of a Supernal that appeals, and building a concept around it that is evocative. If I think the concept fits a different caste I bump up against a rule telling me No. There are RAW ways to deal with this, but I don\u2019t really want to do them because the character doesn\u2019t feel accurate to what I intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:04:48-07:00","id":1306994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306914#post1306914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the point is more, &amp;quot;Supernal doesn't matter as much as people are making it out to.&amp;quot; Supernal matters because it lets you gain access to higher level Charms early, and that's a significant impact on play. It's just something that isn't essential, and something that matters less and less as time goes on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.<br /> Certainly in the Essence 4 and 5 games I play, Supernal is pretty irrelevant, but I assume it's more of a thing at lower levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:33:49-07:00","id":1307010,"title":"","content":"Yep... though the Charm trees also matter at lower Essence. Part of the issue I think is that some Charm trees are varied a lot in how much specialization (and thus how deep you can really afford to go early on with Supernal).<br /> <br /> Like Melee, which is probably going to be your primary offense and defense Ability if you go Supernal with it, plus all the important utility Charms, means trying to rush towards the top of the tree in offense Charms might be leaving your really screwed compared to someone that spread their Charms around more. A master sword user can't just focus on attacking. Meanwhile, over in Athletics, if you want to do the feats of strength tree, rushing to the top of that goes a long way, and sure the rest of Athletics is nice, but you'll have plenty of Charms left to play around anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:38:34-07:00","id":1307014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic#post1306534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can\u2019t be a Twilight making an academic study of strategy with War.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Dawn caste admiral.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Zenith writing holy commandments into stone.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Dawn caste battle-sorcerer<br /> Burning Exorcism Technique is absolutely unavailable to a Zenith at chargen, as is any kind of high-essence medicine effect. Exorcism and healing the faithful isn\u2019t in theme for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one of these concepts requires the specific Ability in question to have the character's STRONGEST charms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:34:02-07:00","id":1307042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306935#post1306935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Really, I consider all 3 for those rules to be absolutely terrible, so I avoid them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd sooner go for a confluence of rules that produces a nonsensical result?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:06:27-07:00","id":1307056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307042#post1307042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd sooner go for a confluence of rules that produces a nonsensical result?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll let you know when it comes up. 20+ years of role playing, still hasn't happened. Seriously, I've never seen a campaign last more than a session after an invocation of the &quot;Orichalcum&quot; Rule, or as I call it the Abusive DM rule. But let's not talk about it. This is a tangent that only bad things can come from, and I shouldn't have started it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T18:12:06-07:00","id":1307084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306846#post1306846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Swan came from the West, didn't he?<br /> <br /> He seems to me to have been more of a world-walker than he was a behind-the-scenes operator.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Swan's greatest emphasis in past editions was on Martial Arts over everything else, with a sideline in being really acrobatic and light on his feet. He was the Snake Style poster boy since 1e, in fact. He was also a Coral Warrior-Diplomat, which meant while being a dashing man of action, he was also a behind the scenes operator in most respects - negotiator of treaties, broker of business deals, handler of contracts with unruly privateers. He also manages to get his &quot;world walker&quot; thing, if any, done with basement ratings in Ride and Sail and no Charms in either Ability. His primary emphasis in Eclipse-dom seems to be Socialize, and then Bureaucracy. The Eclipse in the popular eye who seems to use Sail most is Admiral Sand, and he still has a higher Bureaucracy rating than Sail in his original appearance in CB:E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T18:23:05-07:00","id":1307087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307084#post1307084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Swan's greatest emphasis in past editions was on Martial Arts over everything else, with a sideline in being really acrobatic and light on his feet. He was the Snake Style poster boy since 1e, in fact. He was also a Coral Warrior-Diplomat, which meant while being a dashing man of action, he was also a behind the scenes operator in most respects - negotiator of treaties, broker of business deals, handler of contracts with unruly privateers. He also manages to get his &quot;world walker&quot; thing, if any, done with basement ratings in Ride and Sail and no Charms in either Ability. His primary emphasis in Eclipse-dom seems to be Socialize, and then Bureaucracy. The Eclipse in the popular eye who seems to use Sail most is Admiral Sand, and he still has a higher Bureaucracy rating than Sail in his original appearance in CB:E.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly losing track of what this tangent between us is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T21:55:23-07:00","id":1307140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306935#post1306935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rule zero isn't exactly useful for discussion in a public forum. The rules form the common basis by which all discussions take place. Even in private use the golden rule can serve as an obstacle to bringing in new people to game as they understand the game in terms of the published rules. Really, I consider all 3 for those rules to be absolutely terrible, so I avoid them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted 3e I think is notable in that it puts the Golden Rule et al. as the very firs three rules in the entire Systems Chapter. So while you have your own philosophy on such things, I think that there is osmething to be discussed in their context since the original devs were pretty clear that the rules are not universally perfect for every instance and for every table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T22:26:16-07:00","id":1307144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307140#post1307140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted 3e I think is notable in that it puts the Golden Rule et al. as the very firs three rules in the entire Systems Chapter. So while you have your own philosophy on such things, I think that there is osmething to be discussed in their context since the original devs were pretty clear that the rules are not universally perfect for every instance and for every table.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of games that put them as the first paragraph of the book, that doesn't change a damned thing about those rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T23:59:31-07:00","id":1307160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306663#post1306663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If War had more impact on the naval mechanics, then the Dawn admiral concept would be War Supernal and Sail Favored, and it wouldn't feel weird at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it would feel more like we're used to thinking of naval warfare, sure.<br /> <br /> But War does have significant impact, just not obvious in the naval mechanics, because the boarding action plays out as a clash between battle groups.<br /> <br /> The separation of the roles of military captain and sailing master, and the centrality of boarding actions, is quite consistent with historical naval warfare of the eras Exalted tries to evoke. Sinking enemy ships by shooting them with shipboard weapons didn't become a practical tactic until the gunpowder age, and it was a long time after that until you got anything that looked like the naval warfare we think of as typical. The military captain who also knew how sail was a 17th Century Dutch innovation (at least in Europe), as were things like the line of battle, &quot;crossing the T&quot;, and other maneuver-ships-as-a-group tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T01:07:20-07:00","id":1307173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307160#post1307160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But War does have significant impact, just not obvious in the naval mechanics, because the boarding action plays out as a clash between battle groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only a clash between BGs if both sides are sending BGs into the fray. It reverts to normal combat.<br /> <br /> What I'm talking about is something as simple as having Boarding Actions be Sail or War, and count as Strategic Maneuvers so War Charms that enhance those can apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T04:18:34-07:00","id":1307194,"title":"","content":"Leaving aside the question of whether Supernal is a particularly good mechanic, not all abilities are created equal in regards to it. Many Solar Charm sets don't really grow into more than 'throw bucket-loads of dice cheaper and break caps', which, while good of course, don't really compare to those abilities which open up entire new ways of doing things and character concepts at the essence 3+ level, or, alternatively, those which intersect heavily with the combat engine.<br /> <br /> In short, you have 'good' Supernals and 'bad' Supernals. If approached like this, it reduces the number of possible picks per Caste significantly.<br /> <br /> Keeping that in mind, I lean more towards letting Caste abilities and especially roles give identity to the Caste concept. Nothing breaks if you don't limit Supernal choice, imho not even Caste themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T08:13:01-07:00","id":1307221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1306867#post1306867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, that's always the case. The thread is really whether it's good for the game to change. Of course, at your table you can change anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then No, I don't think the game needs to be officially changed. It is a bit late at this point anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T17:27:42-07:00","id":1307349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307087#post1307087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm honestly losing track of what this tangent between us is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>The centrality of concepts as divided by Caste and Caste Ability selection, surely. As another example of the Eclipse's blind spot for travel, consider that Survival is out for them, even if it would make sense for them to bond with riding beasts and engage in orienteering for overland travel, which is the sort of travel they'd most rely upon in their present milieu. Not so much when flying machines and such were commonplace, perhaps, but that world isn't the one they're in now. And, if you suggest that maybe they should have Survival, people object to it on the grounds that it makes them too much like Chosen of Journeys, even though Chosen of Journeys and Sidereals in general do very different things with Survival* and Solars get a fluid 5 out of 8 choice now, so an Eclipse could easily just get into, say, Linguistics, Presence, and Bureaucracy and be very much the opposite of a Chosen of Journeys with respect to most basic capabilities in this hypothetical &quot;Eclipses get Survival instead of Larceny&quot; scenario. <br /> <br /> *Some other Sidereal Charms that fall under Bananasid auspices could have a slight feel of duplicated function in a few places, since Ride does do fast travel for Sidereals and aids with familiar-bonding, but Sidereal Sail is really, really different from Solar Sail, and Eclipses never touched Thrown, so I'm still not seeing that close of an overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:36:56-07:00","id":1307362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307349#post1307349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The centrality of concepts as divided by Caste and Caste Ability selection, surely.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be because it's late and I've had a particularly trying day, but whaaa? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another example of the Eclipse's blind spot for travel</div> </div> </div> </div>They have what now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">consider that Survival is out for them, even if it would make sense for them to bond with riding beasts and engage in orienteering for overland travel, which is the sort of travel they'd most rely upon in their present milieu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's strictly necessary for the riding animals stuff, but for general navigation...<br /> <br /> It does feel as though Presence could be dropped for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much when flying machines and such were commonplace, perhaps, but that world isn't the one they're in now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't think that was necessarily all-encompassing in the First Age either.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:39:04-07:00","id":1307363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307349#post1307349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The centrality of concepts as divided by Caste and Caste Ability selection, surely. As another example of the Eclipse's blind spot for travel, consider that Survival is out for them, even if it would make sense for them to bond with riding beasts and engage in orienteering for overland travel, which is the sort of travel they'd most rely upon in their present milieu. Not so much when flying machines and such were commonplace, perhaps, but that world isn't the one they're in now. And, if you suggest that maybe they should have Survival, people object to it on the grounds that it makes them too much like Chosen of Journeys, even though Chosen of Journeys and Sidereals in general do very different things with Survival* and Solars get a fluid 5 out of 8 choice now, so an Eclipse could easily just get into, say, Linguistics, Presence, and Bureaucracy and be very much the opposite of a Chosen of Journeys with respect to most basic capabilities in this hypothetical &quot;Eclipses get Survival instead of Larceny&quot; scenario. <br /> <br /> *Some other Sidereal Charms that fall under Bananasid auspices could have a slight feel of duplicated function in a few places, since Ride does do fast travel for Sidereals and aids with familiar-bonding, but Sidereal Sail is really, really different from Solar Sail, and Eclipses never touched Thrown, so I'm still not seeing that close of an overlap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly we'd have to see what sidereals get. Right now solars are defined by supernal, lunars are generalists and a dragon-blooded are defined by aura. <br /> <br /> Sidereals are going to be at the celestial level but without knowing jow their charmset currently works we won't know how well they can dip. Using their only functional 1e charmset, sidereals were intended to cherry pick a bunch of charms from a bunch of trees not lim8ted to their own purview. So we'll have to see how that goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:56:48-07:00","id":1307370,"title":"","content":"from what Vance thought of it a couple months back, the Sid plan was to give them some very powerful charms but in small number and not much growth. That while they can have a starter charm that is comparable to e3 once they actually get to that point their growth with their natural charmsets will slowly stop. Thus if Sids want to expand out from their they would have to do so from SMA. Or in anycase thats how I think I remember it going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T19:00:05-07:00","id":1307372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307370#post1307370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">from what Vance thought of it a couple months back, the Sid plan was to give them some very powerful charms but in small number and not much growth. That while they can have a starter charm that is comparable to e3 once they actually get to that point their growth with their natural charmsets will slowly stop. Thus if Sids want to expand out from their they would have to do so from SMA. Or in anycase thats how I think I remember it going.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want the limited charmset but I hope they aren't FORCED to go into SMA. I really hope that they have another option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T19:02:14-07:00","id":1307373,"title":"","content":"well, theirs always artifacts. their a good buy for anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T19:05:02-07:00","id":1307375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic#post1306534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To avoid derailing The aura thread more than it\u2019s already been derailed.<br /> <br /> So personally I don\u2019t see much value in limiting the supernal to the caste abilities? It basically massively reduces the scope of character concepts you can have at chargen, often with bizarre exclusions.<br /> <br /> You can\u2019t be a Twilight making an academic study of strategy with War.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Dawn caste admiral.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Zenith writing holy commandments into stone.<br /> You can\u2019t be a Dawn caste battle-sorcerer<br /> Burning Exorcism Technique is absolutely unavailable to a Zenith at chargen, as is any kind of high-essence medicine effect. Exorcism and healing the faithful isn\u2019t in theme for them?<br /> <br /> To be clear, I\u2019m not badmouthing the caste ability distribution. I think it works just fine. I just don\u2019t get why Supernal being limited to it is necessary or helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty OK with all of those examples to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T19:12:51-07:00","id":1307380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307373#post1307373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, theirs always artifacts. their a good buy for anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just hope astrology is viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T19:16:00-07:00","id":1307382,"title":"","content":"This all seems kinda odd to me as Eclipses have Ride, which is far more useful (esp. as a Supernal) for someone traveling normal routes rather than going through the wilderness all the time for some reason. The Survival Charms are nice, but the higher Essence ones don't really scream anything the Eclipse need thematically. They're served just fine going Ride Supernal with Survival as Favored if they want to focus on &quot;bond with riding beasts&quot; esp. since Ride can transfer to new mounts fairly easily compared to the Survival familiar tree; though of course both combined is really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T20:02:24-07:00","id":1307392,"title":"","content":"Eh I'm not sure, Ride does give you some useful charms for going off terrain, that while not a lot is basically all you pretty much need, capping off at Sometimes Horses Fly Approach where they can run anything from water to clouds, combine that with the speed bonuses you will have a Rider blitzing past the place no matter where they are. Nights having Ride seems more odder to me tbh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T20:45:26-07:00","id":1307399,"title":"","content":"The thing Ride lacks is the navigation/orienteering aspect. Ride lets you go pretty much anywhere if you go through the Charms, but you still have to know how to get there (of course, that's not hard, and unless you're facing magical opposition).<br /> <br /> Nights having Ride is, I think, to get away from Nights-as-Ninjas, and allow for wider outlaw concept inspirations. Ride is really useful for a Night that's more of a bandit than a ninja, esp with their ability to get out of fights fast.. and steal mounts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T05:44:31-07:00","id":1307446,"title":"","content":"The thing I have always wanted to play since 3rd edition came out is a socialize supernal Zenith with the persona charms, to allow you to become those whose intimacies you have taken on, but alas Socialize is not caste for Zeniths. I think on balance that the caste-only probably makes for the best default rule to prevent things that could be abusive (twilight survival shenanigans) or otherwise problematic (Nobody cares about playing a dawn if other castes can get their stuff). However since this is a game with actual people we can chat with STs about it and hopefully work it out. Most of the concepts I have seen in this thread seem fine to me and I would allow as an ST, but I'm glad the rule is in place and deviating from it is optional rather than the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T06:19:43-07:00","id":1307450,"title":"","content":"You could maybe make an argument for castes getting certain martial arts as supernal if they fit their themes, like say nights getting ebon shadow and black claw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T07:46:14-07:00","id":1307471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307446#post1307446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing I have always wanted to play since 3rd edition came out is a socialize supernal Zenith with the persona charms, to allow you to become those whose intimacies you have taken on, but alas Socialize is not caste for Zeniths. I think on balance that the caste-only probably makes for the best default rule to prevent things that could be abusive (twilight survival shenanigans) or otherwise problematic (Nobody cares about playing a dawn if other castes can get their stuff). However since this is a game with actual people we can chat with STs about it and hopefully work it out. Most of the concepts I have seen in this thread seem fine to me and I would allow as an ST, but I'm glad the rule is in place and deviating from it is optional rather than the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is ultimately my view. I think that it's good there by default. If it were not so, you'd get a lot of caste dilution that the devs don't want, so keeping it stricter is a good way to keep it as a baseline. But individual players and STs should be able to argue their case, which again, is what the whole point of the Three Rules at the start say and I think is generally a sign of good ST negoitations anyhow to know hwen and where it's appropriate. I by default probably would argue no, but I think a case can be made for yes if presented well enough. It's a cooperative thing between ST and PCs anyhow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T08:37:37-07:00","id":1307484,"title":"","content":"What could actually be an abusive combo?<br /> <br /> This Twilight-Survival gets mentioned, but I mean, survival charms tacked on an essence 1-3 spirit leaves me kinda shrugging and going 'what's the big deal?'. There are definitely gamebreaking shenanigans to be done with Survival, but, really, applying your survival pet charms on a blood ape is hardly at that level.<br /> <br /> I also really have trouble comprehending this Caste dilution talk? What gets diluted actually? <br /> <br /> I can easily imagine a member of any Caste have <i>any </i>Supernal, and it is actually a rewarding exercise to do so. Also, I often find that this conversation boils down to the following:<br /> <br /> A not-Dawn having Supernal melee, archery or brawl is somehow completely invalidating Dawns. Because why else play Dawns?<br /> <br /> This is wrong on so, <i>so</i> many levels.<br /> <br /> Dawns are nothing more than the possibility of choosing higher essence melee charms? And for all Castes from essence 3+ on Supernals are dropping off in importance, so, suddenly your Caste is also less important? Meh. Not buying it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T08:47:41-07:00","id":1307489,"title":"","content":"Dawn have a history of being the &quot;fighty caste&quot; in name only. In 2e zenith was usually a better choice.<br /> <br /> Third edition firmly cemented their place as ass-kickers extraordinaire, and their monopoly on supernal combat abilities is a big part of this. <br /> <br /> Caste abilities alone don't really <i>do </i>anything. You get five caste abilities, and five favoured abilities. You can put those 5 favoured into the abilities of another caste. If supernal can go anywhere then there's no real difference between those castes, aside from a few anima abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:19:11-07:00","id":1307518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307489#post1307489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dawn have a history of being the &quot;fighty caste&quot; in name only. In 2e zenith was usually a better choice.<br /> <br /> Third edition firmly cemented their place as ass-kickers extraordinaire, and their monopoly on supernal combat abilities is a big part of this.<br /> <br /> Caste abilities alone don't really <i>do </i>anything. You get five caste abilities, and five favoured abilities. You can put those 5 favoured into the abilities of another caste. If supernal can go anywhere then there's no real difference between those castes, aside from a few anima abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, supernals essentially signify the things that your character can do that are absolutely better than <i>anyone else in Creation</i> right out of the gate (note that you don't need to invest heavily, but that's your choice).<br /> <br /> Dawns are the only ones who can become the worlds greatest swordsman (archer, brawler, throwing, etc) right out of the gate. <br /> <br /> Honestly, to me, supernals define the role that each caste plays far more strongly than the caste abilities. This is especially true of those abilities that are <i>exclusive</i> to each caste. <br /> <br /> Dawns: Peerless warriors, masters of sword, bow, fists, and thrown. <br /> Zenith: The world's greatest survivors/and pokemon trainers<br /> Twilight: Best at craft and medicine. Period<br /> Night: Most stealthy bastards to ever walk the earth <br /> Eclipse: Unbeatable... sailing prowess?<br /> <br /> So I'd give an Eclipse a little more wiggle room than the others as to taking non-typical supernals since their 'thing' is pretty niche. Then again, I think their caste anima powers are probably the most relevant to their caste's role compared to every other caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:26:14-07:00","id":1307521,"title":"","content":"On further thought I really like that Dawns Don't get Athletics as a Caste.<br /> <br /> If they did, Dawn would be a signifier closer to Full Moon, of a caste of people with supreme physical prowess (even with War).<br /> <br /> While that's not a BAD thing, the fact that Dawns don't get it makes it clear Dawns aren't about physical actions or physicality, they're about combat, war, and fighting. It might make Awareness a bit weirder as a Caste ability, but I can still see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:35:59-07:00","id":1307525,"title":"","content":"Eh, as the ability of the bodyguard who cuts down an unseen assassin hidden behind the wall before they can even draw their poisoned blade, and given its' far closer ties [Join Battle, avoiding Ambush, one of which you do every single combat and the other of which gives your enemy a massive advantage if you can't] to combat than Athletics [Rush, ....?; a relatively situational action primarily used if someone is trying to get away] I think it's a fine choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 04-24-2019, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:39:24-07:00","id":1307528,"title":"","content":"Eclipses being able to Mega Man spirit charms feels more characteristic of them than their possible supernals. They get more thematic breadth at the cost of a real niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T11:11:19-07:00","id":1307536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307518#post1307518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, supernals essentially signify the things that your character can do that are absolutely better than <i>anyone else in Creation</i> right out of the gate (note that you don't need to invest heavily, but that's your choice).<br /> <br /> Dawns are the only ones who can become the worlds greatest swordsman (archer, brawler, throwing, etc) right out of the gate.<br /> <br /> Honestly, to me, supernals define the role that each caste plays far more strongly than the caste abilities. This is especially true of those abilities that are <i>exclusive</i> to each caste.<br /> <br /> Dawns: Peerless warriors, masters of sword, bow, fists, and thrown.<br /> Zenith: The world's greatest survivors/and pokemon trainers<br /> Twilight: Best at craft and medicine. Period<br /> Night: Most stealthy bastards to ever walk the earth<br /> Eclipse: Unbeatable... sailing prowess?<br /> <br /> So I'd give an Eclipse a little more wiggle room than the others as to taking non-typical supernals since their 'thing' is pretty niche. Then again, I think their caste anima powers are probably the most relevant to their caste's role compared to every other caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah one note the Zeniths get Survival less because the caste is for tamers and survivors, rather its supposed to represent the caste as martyrs and prophets in religions where they spend ungodly amount of time in the wilderness by themselves, while all the animals around them just makes way to them and obey them, at the max. Zeniths are Noah in short.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 04-24-2019, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T13:00:21-07:00","id":1307562,"title":"","content":"Zeniths also get Performance Supernal to themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T13:55:09-07:00","id":1307577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307362#post1307362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might be because it's late and I've had a particularly trying day, but whaaa?</div> </div> </div> </div>I stated my assertion that Sail wasn't really a defining Eclipse thing since they were more quiet influence types. You seemed to disagree on the grounds of Eclipses being world-walkers. The two aren't mutually exclusive, but it seems that travel isn't strongly emphasized in an edition where you can ditch Ride and Sail for two out of three of Larceny, Presence and Occult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have what now? </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'll tell you what they don't - Survival!&quot;<br /> <br /> (Horrifying Abridged Popo Laugh)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think it's strictly necessary for the riding animals stuff, but for general navigation...<br /> <br /> It does feel as though Presence could be dropped for it. </div> </div> </div>Presence got a lot loaded onto it as a general, all-purpose active one to one social Ability, so probably not as the system stands. That's why I specified tossing out Larceny as one of the three additional choices. Eclipses have their own twist on how to be a spy, and it's squarely in Socialize.<br /> <br /> [/quote]<br /> Eh, I don't think that was necessarily all-encompassing in the First Age either.<br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I was probably hung up on the point of &quot;Sail vehicles that aren't watercraft&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T14:11:50-07:00","id":1307582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307577#post1307577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I stated my assertion that Sail wasn't really a defining Eclipse thing since they were more quiet influence types. You seemed to disagree on the grounds of Eclipses being world-walkers. The two aren't mutually exclusive, but it seems that travel isn't strongly emphasized in an edition where you can ditch Ride and Sail for two out of three of Larceny, Presence and Occult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Castes can be broad. That includes giving players the option to not include every part of them in every character concept.<br /> <br /> Prince Diamond presumably not being a sailor specifically does not detract from how his ethos focuses on the aspect of the world-walker, anymore than a Dawn Caste who is laser focused on Single Point Style is not being a proper warrior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I specified tossing out Larceny as one of the three additional choices. Eclipses have their own twist on how to be a spy, and it's squarely in Socialize.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the presence of Larceny as being less about the spying and more about insinuation into the underworld. I think Larceny sufficiently distinguishes itself from Socialize on that count, and where it doesn't, it invites a measure of suspension of disbelief (so to speak).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T17:07:54-07:00","id":1307621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307562#post1307562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeniths also get Performance Supernal to themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they do! Good catch","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T19:22:46-07:00","id":1307657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307582#post1307582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Castes can be broad. That includes giving players the option to not include every part of them in every character concept.<br /> <br /> Prince Diamond presumably not being a sailor specifically does not detract from how his ethos focuses on the aspect of the world-walker, anymore than a Dawn Caste who is laser focused on Single Point Style is not being a proper warrior.</div> </div> </div> </div>This wasn't about not being a sailor meaning that you were being a poor Eclipse - quite the opposite, really, I was originally arguing that Sail was not really necessary to be an Eclipse, nor a signature capacity that only they should have. Their signature capacity is in sealing oaths and diplomatic immunity, with a sideline into learning designated spirit Charms (and that last one is even broken down a bit by certain Occult Charms); none of this requires Sail, though a sailor might find some of it useful. Then, there are probably a lot of capabilities that a sailor might find useful, like being able to frighten off pirates with a mean look, or dampening an injury. The sea is harsh and unforgiving, and everyone in the West has to deal with it constantly (even if you're on an island, the maritime influence still reaches inland).<br /> <br /> Hmm... regional Supernal Abilities, by any chance? That would make them an additional option, rather than a mandate, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see the presence of Larceny as being less about the spying and more about insinuation into the underworld. I think Larceny sufficiently distinguishes itself from Socialize on that count, and where it doesn't, it invites a measure of suspension of disbelief (so to speak). </div> </div> </div>Socialize seems like it could encompass that in its typical course of finding out what people want and playing close to the chest with your own ideals and desires, as well as projecting a different air apart from your real feelings on a matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T20:31:06-07:00","id":1307668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307657#post1307657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This wasn't about not being a sailor meaning that you were being a poor Eclipse - quite the opposite, really, I was originally arguing that Sail was not really necessary to be an Eclipse, nor a signature capacity that only they should have. Their signature capacity is in sealing oaths and diplomatic immunity, with a sideline into learning designated spirit Charms (and that last one is even broken down a bit by certain Occult Charms); none of this requires Sail, though a sailor might find some of it useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds very reductive to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Socialize seems like it could encompass that in its typical course of finding out what people want and playing close to the chest with your own ideals and desires, as well as projecting a different air apart from your real feelings on a matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're turning down the invitation.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I recalled also having a sense of Larceny having a place in the confluence between diplomatic immunity and the world-walker/explorer angles in conveying a sense of Solars of the Eclipse Caste being folks you can't really prevent from going where they please, or their duties take them. I have this image of a demon prince desperately trying to prevent an Eclipse from going anywhere near them and being obligated to treat with them, and the Eclipse can handily ignore their walls and doors and bars to invite themselves for dinner.<br /> <br /> Larceny is of course a bit bigger than that, but a lot of Abilities are bigger than the Castes they're attached to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T11:21:05-07:00","id":1307806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307621#post1307621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they do! Good catch</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I saw quite a few Eclipse Caste concepts that revolved around Performance get a little caught off-guard by Supernal, so I'm sympathetic to the idea that sometimes this is an appropriate use of the Golden Rule.<br /> <br /> I think part of why this is an issue is that some people have it in their head that a Supernal Ability has a deeper significance than which charm tree you\u2019ve got a head start in and that you're locked out of being \u2018the best\u2019 at something without it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:25:50-07:00","id":1307895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307668#post1307668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds very reductive to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the only capacities that a Caste has that no other Caste gets are the anima powers. Maybe they should have been the premiere niche mechanic instead of Supernal Abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you're turning down the invitation.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I recalled also having a sense of Larceny having a place in the confluence between diplomatic immunity and the world-walker/explorer angles in conveying a sense of Solars of the Eclipse Caste being folks you can't really prevent from going where they please, or their duties take them. I have this image of a demon prince desperately trying to prevent an Eclipse from going anywhere near them and being obligated to treat with them, and the Eclipse can handily ignore their walls and doors and bars to invite themselves for dinner.<br /> <br /> Larceny is of course a bit bigger than that, but a lot of Abilities are bigger than the Castes they're attached to. </div> </div> </div>I thought that the Night Caste was the Caste that was supposed to go everywhere and couldn't be prevented from doing so. Eclipses are rule-masters; they know how to bend them, but they still have to abide by them, which means that true unavoidability is off the table; at some point, the host will refuse you, and at that point, continuing on is B&amp;E, and will void your status as an envoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:11:46-07:00","id":1307953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1307521#post1307521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On further thought I really like that Dawns Don't get Athletics as a Caste.<br /> <br /> If they did, Dawn would be a signifier closer to Full Moon, of a caste of people with supreme physical prowess (even with War).<br /> <br /> While that's not a BAD thing, the fact that Dawns don't get it makes it clear Dawns aren't about physical actions or physicality, they're about combat, war, and fighting. It might make Awareness a bit weirder as a Caste ability, but I can still see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with this. I also kind of like how it went into Zenith instead, as I think there's soemthing that the Zeniths are the ones hwo can as a whole pull off the &quot;exemplar&quot; thing. You could in thoery go with Athletics, Integrity, Lore, Presence, and Resistance, and just play-up being the most pfit, wise, and personable person in the world. I think that sometimes it's not just the indivdiaul Caste Ability but also to be ocnsidered the Abilities hollistically and hwo they might synergize wiht a particular Supernal also.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T10:41:21-07:00","id":1308064,"title":"","content":"An extra on Awareness and Dawns as a note is that a lot of fiction does include warriors with superlative senses. This might include the archer who shoots from miles away, to the Zatoichi-style blind swordsmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T13:04:16-07:00","id":1308095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1308064#post1308064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An extra on Awareness and Dawns as a note is that a lot of fiction does include warriors with superlative senses. This might include the archer who shoots from miles away, to the Zatoichi-style blind swordsmen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To the extent that when one of my players read the castes for the first time, his first thought (and character!) was &quot;I want to be a Dawn Caste blind swordman with Supernal Awareness&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T01:38:19-07:00","id":1308258,"title":"","content":"But what charms let you do that specifically?<br /> You can do it with a Lunar using echolocation (though it costs 1wp a day), but I can't see what the obvious and simple way to do it with Awareness is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T02:02:24-07:00","id":1308261,"title":"","content":"The hearing/touch branch does most of the heavy lifting for a blind swordsman style character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T02:11:12-07:00","id":1308262,"title":"","content":"Specifically?<br /> I'm not asking this to be a dick, it's because I think it's a cool concept but I don't really see what straightforward charm lets you ignore the blindness penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T07:25:29-07:00","id":1308304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306534-the-supernal-must-be-in-caste-mechanic?p=1308262#post1308262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically?<br /> I'm not asking this to be a dick, it's because I think it's a cool concept but I don't really see what straightforward charm lets you ignore the blindness penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't exactly. The Hearing and Touch branch focusses on detecting those hidden from sight. <br /> <br /> However, read the section under Flaws on page 167. Since the flaws are optional and don't cost points of any kind, the player may preselect how and when they affect their character (you can be circumstantially blind, as it were). You can select the Blind flaw if you want to play a swordsman who's preternatural hearing compensates for lack of sight (so their swordfighting does not <i>primarily</i> depend on sight).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T12:32:30-07:00","id":1308368,"title":"","content":"OK:<br /> <br /> Remembering that the Blind penalty only applies to actions that primarily rely on using sight so... just don't use sight.<br /> <br /> The basic build:<br /> <br /> The Danger Sense Merit (more because it's innate rather than strictly necessary, but it makes the benefits of SAM that much better)<br /> <br /> A specialty in Blind Fighting for Melee.<br /> <br /> Sensory Acuity Prana for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> Surprise Anticipation Method to help offset SAP and Eye Harbinger Awareness (also to recoup the special activation of Keen (Sense) Techniques so they're on indefinitely without constantly eating up 6m each).<br /> <br /> Keen Hearing and Touch Technique activated indefinitely so you don't have to activate it as the fight starts. While fighting using hearing and touch, rolling to detect non-hidden enemies is either waved (if ruled low enough difficulty), or a difficulty 1 roll on which you have an automatic 1 Charm success anyway.<br /> <br /> Eyeless Harbinger Awareness gives you a non-Charm dice bonus to JB (which is very nice for our blind swordsman to have), like Sensory Acuity Prana it's a relatively cheap (2m in this setup) scene long Reflexive Charm. The free upgrade with Unsurpassed Hearing and Touch Discipline means that at least out to Medium range you're at Daredevil level senses against things not hiding from you (and you have a tone of bonuses if they are).<br /> <br /> Unsurpassed Hearing and Touch Discipline for the boost to the two previous (plus the -1m cost on all the other hearing/touch Charms, and it's own stuff is fun too if less necessary for the concept.<br /> <br /> At this point we have someone that should pull off the blind swordsman/Daredevil tropes just fine, you haven't eaten up a ton Charms so you have plenty for some Melee or MA stuff depending on how you want to do that. You do need to be Supernal Awareness to pull this off at start.<br /> <br /> Stuff to get sooner rather than later (char-gen can be sooner if you have points to spare!):<br /> <br /> Fast Reflexes because you'll want to eke out every drop of JB you can.<br /> <br /> Studied Ear Espial (very cost effective and doesn't matter why the target is using Stealth to move around, also pre-req), Knowing Beyond Silence (another very cost effective boost to spotting people, great synergy with SAP and SAM, and works with JB too), Living Pulse Perception (situational but automatic success on noticing people or JB against them).<br /> <br /> Keen Taste and Smell Technique (Need it to get back to where the branches converse, and the taste/smell branch has some things worth getting esp. if you don't want to dip to far into more Charm Trees), Foe-Scenting Method (helps deal with crowds, which the hearing/touch stuff doesn't, and gets you the ability to sniff out dematerialized spirits), Unsurpassed Taste and Smell Discipline (expands tracking, -1m to F-SM, limited read intentions with smell)<br /> <br /> Awakening Eye for the massive JB boost.<br /> <br /> Stealth against you is really, really hard, and your JB pool is really big with a lot of dice tricks on it, you can easily have a starting Initiative that can kill with an opening decisive.<br /> <br /> Gravy:<br /> <br /> More specialties for Keen Hearing/Touch to help in more than just combat.<br /> <br /> The rest of hearing/touch and taste/smell because they're good even if not great for fighting for the most part and there are dice caps to consider.<br /> <br /> Eye of the Unconquered Sun, because it's good, and it helps your non-Stealthy friends too.<br /> <br /> Talk to your ST:<br /> <br /> The sight branch, because Keen Sight Technique boosts EotUS, Unsurpassed Sight Discipline on top of the the others means -1m to all Awareness Charm costs (really nice for SAP, AE, and EotUS), and Blink which is frustratingly buried in the sight branch despite applying to any Awareness roll and might actually be worth it despite two Charms you can't use blind before it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}